## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-05-31
Number: 22
Notes: An hourglass 19 wide and 11 high (19 squares in the top and bottom rows, narrowing by one square each side to 9 in the middle row, squares outside shown as _), with shaded squares inside the outline making two X shapes; they are printed shaded, not black, and stand as blocks (#). Number printed in the heading box ("No 22"); the intro calls it "number twenty-one in FUN'S series of cross word puzzles" and the solution, the next week, "cross-word puzzle No. 22". No credit is printed. Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_05_31_90.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_06_07_85.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.
Numbering: across-first


